  "_": "The world's components and the models that draw them, one place (realistic.gd reads it through data.gd; docs/TUNING.md). A placer asks for a component (fence, house_poor, keep...), never a file, so a new art family is an edit here. Shape: Paradox's entity files and RimWorld's ThingDef graphicData. Per component: kind (what the town rules ask for: house, hall, barn, prop, clutter...) and variants. Per variant: model (under res://assets; a folder means its scene.gltf), name (the name placers used before the catalogue, kept while they move over), length (its true longest side in metres: the scale), and optionally strip (parts the land supplies itself), floorCut (game units: triangles under it dropped), stone (no glow), weight (how often it's picked). Order matters: it is the order placers pick in.",
